<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Lint on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/tags/lint/</link><description>Recent content in Lint on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:44:44 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/tags/lint/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Lint and Lint Errors</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/lint/</link><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/lint/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="what-is-lint"&gt;What is lint?&lt;a class="anchor" href="#what-is-lint"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Suppose you write this program:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Done&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Run it. You will see:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;Done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The program works. But look at &lt;code&gt;total&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You calculated it and never used it. Perhaps you meant to print it. Perhaps you no longer need that line.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;JavaScript does not complain, so how would you notice?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We can use a tool to examine the code we have written.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It does not run the program. Instead, it checks the code against a set of rules to identify potential problems , expected style which we are supposed to write programs in and code-quality issues.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>